  "name": "Introduction",
  "problem": "When we subtract a positive number from another positive number, we move towards the left on the number line. \n\nFor example, let's consider the following subtraction problem:\n\n$$\n3 - 5\n$$\n\nTo subtract $5$ from $3,$ we start at $3$ on the number line and move $5$ places to the left.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14132866/assets/57ac1fe7a28ae5fefadf900d2276d499cdccf01df48b819b0aafa5347a2ec506.png)\n\nWhen we do this, we land at $-2.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n3-5 = -2.\n$$",
